IMPORT prelude

-- Three-valued connectives over MAYBE BOOLEAN.  Not law: plumbing, so that a NOTHING ("the text does not answer")
-- from one section is carried into the answer of a section that consults it, and is never turned into FALSE.
--   JUST FALSE with anything is JUST FALSE;  JUST TRUE with JUST TRUE is JUST TRUE;  anything else is NOTHING.
--   JUST TRUE with anything is JUST TRUE;  JUST FALSE with JUST FALSE is JUST FALSE;  anything else is NOTHING.

GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the conjunction` a `and also` b MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF a EQUALS JUST FALSE OR b EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        IF a EQUALS JUST TRUE AND b EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the disjunction` a `or else` b MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF a EQUALS JUST TRUE OR b EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF a EQUALS JUST FALSE AND b EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the negation of` a MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF a EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
        IF a EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- A plain fact as a MAYBE BOOLEAN, for use beside a consulted rule's answer.
GIVEN x IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the fact` x MEANS JUST x
